WEBVTT

00:03.160 --> 00:06.232
It's hard to believe after all these years,
we've got a new stepdad.

00:07.160 --> 00:09.071
I give it six months.

00:09.240 --> 00:10.355
Come on, we like Teddy.

00:10.520 --> 00:13.398
That's why I'm only giving it six months.
I'm rooting for him.

00:14.400 --> 00:16.755
Still, you have to admit,
it was a beautiful ceremony.

00:16.920 --> 00:18.876
The bride and groom, the sun setting.

00:19.040 --> 00:20.268
The dead butterflies.

00:24.560 --> 00:27.313
Remind me to call the butterfly people
first thing Monday.

00:30.880 --> 00:32.598
What are you doing?

00:39.240 --> 00:40.275
Nothing.

00:40.680 --> 00:43.638
We don't eat from the cake
until we cut the cake.

00:43.800 --> 00:44.994
But I'm still hungry.

00:45.160 --> 00:46.354
Have some cheese.

00:46.520 --> 00:47.873
Have we cut the cheese?

00:49.560 --> 00:51.039
Get it?

00:52.160 --> 00:53.229
Hey, stepbrother.

00:53.400 --> 00:55.311
Change your mind
about wanting to marry me?

00:55.480 --> 00:56.595
Not at all.

00:56.760 --> 00:59.797
Wanna go upstairs and get a head start
on our honeymoon?

00:59.960 --> 01:01.439
You keep rubbing against me...

01:01.600 --> 01:04.512
...I'll be able to catch my
mom's garter without my hands.

01:07.920 --> 01:09.876
- Charlie.
- What?

01:10.040 --> 01:11.189
At your mother's wedding?

01:11.920 --> 01:13.319
Yeah.

01:14.520 --> 01:16.590
I ain't cleaning it up.

01:18.920 --> 01:20.956
Boy, this is pretty kinky.

01:21.120 --> 01:22.189
Kinky good or kinky bad?

01:22.360 --> 01:24.351
There's a kinky bad?

01:25.200 --> 01:26.679
Watch your elbow.

01:26.840 --> 01:29.035
That's not my elbow.

01:29.200 --> 01:30.349
Charlie.

01:31.000 --> 01:33.070
It's not that either.

01:35.680 --> 01:37.079
Daddy?

01:37.240 --> 01:38.355
This is awkward.

01:38.760 --> 01:40.751
Daddy, are you okay?

01:41.240 --> 01:44.118
- What's wrong with him?
- I don't know.

01:46.720 --> 01:48.119
Well?

01:48.280 --> 01:49.633
This might be a mood breaker.

02:06.920 --> 02:09.195
So are you a friend of the bride
or the groom?

02:09.760 --> 02:11.876
Well, the bride is my mother, so...

02:12.040 --> 02:13.519
The groom.

02:13.920 --> 02:15.273
Hey, how do you like my house?

02:15.680 --> 02:17.113
Oh, it's beautiful.

02:18.440 --> 02:21.398
- Alan, I have to talk to you.
- Go away. I've got a shot here.

02:22.480 --> 02:23.754
No, you don't.

02:23.920 --> 02:25.512
- Come upstairs with me.
- Why?

02:25.680 --> 02:26.795
Just come on.

02:26.960 --> 02:28.712
Be right back.

02:29.040 --> 02:30.871
Friend of the bride
or friend of the groom?

02:31.200 --> 02:32.872
Friend of mine.

02:39.240 --> 02:41.834
Oh, my God.

02:42.000 --> 02:43.115
Is he...?

02:43.280 --> 02:45.271
As a doorknob.

02:46.200 --> 02:48.111
- Doorbell?
- Doornail.

02:49.200 --> 02:50.189
He's dead.

02:51.400 --> 02:52.628
I can't believe he's gone.

02:52.800 --> 02:54.392
Courtney, I'm so sorry.

02:55.960 --> 02:58.474
So he was just lying there
with his pants down?

02:59.480 --> 03:02.870
Apparently somebody was giving him
a very special wedding present.

03:03.720 --> 03:05.631
- Mom?
- I don't think so.

03:05.800 --> 03:07.950
She's downstairs
acting as if nothing happened.

03:08.120 --> 03:09.917
And more importantly,
she married the guy.

03:10.080 --> 03:11.559
Why would she bother?

03:13.360 --> 03:15.430
Your mother's looking for you guys.

03:18.360 --> 03:19.475
What's going on?

03:20.200 --> 03:21.918
Teddy's dead.

03:24.760 --> 03:26.876
Yeah, that's a stiffy.

03:28.240 --> 03:30.310
We have got a real problem here.

03:30.480 --> 03:31.959
What do you mean "we"?

04:02.200 --> 04:04.634
Oh, this is just gonna suck.

04:12.440 --> 04:16.035
Thank you, thank you. Now, this
next song you may remember...

04:16.200 --> 04:18.634
...from the hit movie &lt;i>Ghost.&lt;/i>

04:25.120 --> 04:26.269
Mom?

04:28.080 --> 04:29.274
Mom, we gotta talk to you.

04:30.360 --> 04:31.395
What?

04:33.920 --> 04:34.989
It's about Teddy.

04:35.440 --> 04:38.000
Where is he?
This is supposed to be a duet.

04:42.720 --> 04:46.872
Yeah, well, from now on, I'm afraid
you're gonna be working alone.

04:47.040 --> 04:50.555
You son of a bitch.

04:51.320 --> 04:53.993
So you weren't the one who was...?

04:54.160 --> 04:57.675
Of course not.
I already married the man.

05:01.040 --> 05:05.352
I just can't believe he'd cheat on me
on our wedding day.

05:05.520 --> 05:08.637
Excuse me,
my father is lying here dead.

05:08.800 --> 05:12.156
With his pants around his ankles
and lipstick on his hoo-hoo.

05:13.440 --> 05:16.477
Oh, my, what happened in here?

05:18.000 --> 05:20.878
Berta, my husband is dead.

05:21.480 --> 05:23.630
As a doornail.

05:26.000 --> 05:27.638
Has anybody called the cops?

05:28.920 --> 05:30.239
You might wanna consider it...

05:30.400 --> 05:34.029
...because you only got a limited window
before he starts stinking up the joint.

05:35.040 --> 05:36.155
I'll make the calls.

05:36.320 --> 05:38.390
- No, Mom, you don't have to.
- Yes, I do.

05:38.560 --> 05:40.471
I'm his wife.

05:40.800 --> 05:44.713
Now, please, would you all just
give me a moment alone with him?

05:44.880 --> 05:46.711
- Of course.
- Sure, Mom.

05:47.120 --> 05:50.590
So who do you suppose
was smoking Teddy's sausage?

05:50.760 --> 05:53.115
Berta, that is my father in there.

05:53.280 --> 05:54.315
Okay.

05:54.480 --> 05:57.517
So who do you suppose
was smoking your father's sausage?

05:58.600 --> 06:00.113
Oh, Teddy.

06:00.520 --> 06:03.512
My dear, dear Teddy.

06:10.240 --> 06:11.832
Hello.

06:12.160 --> 06:14.879
This is Evelyn Harper Leopold.

06:15.840 --> 06:18.513
I booked my honeymoon with you.

06:19.160 --> 06:20.673
Yes.

06:20.840 --> 06:23.718
Two business-class tickets to Paris.

06:25.360 --> 06:29.751
I need to exchange them
for one first-class ticket to Fiji.

06:31.400 --> 06:33.277
Sure, I'll hold.

06:34.560 --> 06:37.632
This is a crime scene,
so you're just gonna have to be patient.

06:37.800 --> 06:40.951
We'll need statements from
each of you before you can leave.

06:42.560 --> 06:46.314
Anyway, I guess what I'm saying is that
there's a lesson to be learned here.

06:46.760 --> 06:49.672
Life is precious and no one really knows
how long we've got.

06:51.120 --> 06:53.873
So it's important to be grateful
for each day.

06:55.400 --> 06:58.153
So if they're not gonna cut the cake,
can I have some now?

06:58.320 --> 06:59.992
Aren't you full?

07:07.880 --> 07:09.279
No.

07:10.920 --> 07:12.114
Take a look at his pants.

07:15.600 --> 07:17.750
The belt is buckled on an unworn hole.

07:17.920 --> 07:19.148
Someone re-dressed him.

07:20.000 --> 07:21.228
Any of you touch the body?

07:24.000 --> 07:25.672
Interesting.

07:26.040 --> 07:29.555
We've got some peri-mortem
ecchymosis on the posterior occiput.

07:30.680 --> 07:33.638
That means a bruise
on the back of the head.

07:33.800 --> 07:36.758
And yet you still couldn't get
into medical school.

07:38.200 --> 07:39.838
So much for time of death.

07:40.000 --> 07:43.117
Looks like our boy here had some
sexual activity before he bought it.

07:43.640 --> 07:46.313
Hit the light.
I'm gonna check for semen.

07:53.040 --> 07:55.190
My God.

07:55.360 --> 07:57.999
It's like a Jackson Pollock painting.

08:01.320 --> 08:04.835
The ceiling fan's actually a cute story.

08:10.120 --> 08:12.270
- Coffee?
- Thanks.

08:12.440 --> 08:15.000
- So Mr. Harper...
- Call me Charlie.

08:15.600 --> 08:18.239
- And you are?
- Interested in how you found the body.

08:18.400 --> 08:21.198
Oh, right to it, huh?

08:21.720 --> 08:25.918
Okay, well, what have you heard?

08:27.480 --> 08:28.993
That's not how we do this.

08:29.160 --> 08:31.310
You tell me what happened.

08:32.080 --> 08:33.399
All right.

08:33.560 --> 08:36.757
I went upstairs to use the bathroom
and there he was.

08:41.920 --> 08:44.115
Oh, no.

08:44.720 --> 08:46.472
Teddy.

08:48.160 --> 08:50.390
So you're saying you were alone
when you found him?

08:50.560 --> 08:53.233
Well, technically aren't we all alone?

08:55.600 --> 08:58.239
You know, I'm finding that tank top
awfully distracting.

09:05.360 --> 09:06.839
Is that police issue?

09:12.560 --> 09:13.788
Mr. Harper, are you aware...

09:13.960 --> 09:17.430
...that making a false statement
to the police is a crime?

09:18.360 --> 09:19.509
Slap-on-the-wrist crime...

09:19.680 --> 09:22.558
...or pack-my-bags-and-tape-my-butt-shut
crime?

09:25.400 --> 09:28.790
Hey, I like it when it's gift-wrapped.

09:32.080 --> 09:35.231
Okay, okay, I wasn't alone.
I was with Courtney.

09:35.640 --> 09:36.914
- Why'd you lie?
- Oh, come on.

09:37.080 --> 09:40.197
I was trying to nail my stepsister
at my mother's wedding.

09:40.880 --> 09:43.519
Lying seemed the classy way to go.

09:45.040 --> 09:46.109
Did you touch the body?

09:46.280 --> 09:48.271
I was all over her body.

09:50.960 --> 09:52.473
Oh, you mean Teddy?

09:52.640 --> 09:55.029
No, no, no.
Not after I knew he was there.

09:55.200 --> 09:57.236
Who do you suppose
pulled up his pants?

09:58.680 --> 10:01.638
Are you thinking whoever pulled
them up is the one who killed him?

10:01.800 --> 10:03.028
It's crossed our minds.

10:03.200 --> 10:06.192
Oh, gee,
I don't wanna implicate anybody.

10:06.360 --> 10:08.271
Right now,
the only one implicated is you.

10:08.440 --> 10:10.351
Talk to my mother.

10:11.960 --> 10:13.393
What is that? Nondairy creamer?

10:13.560 --> 10:16.597
Just take me to the green mile
and be done with it.

10:17.800 --> 10:18.835
That's all we've got.

10:19.000 --> 10:22.879
Please, this place is crawling with cops.
One of them can't make a Starbucks run?

10:24.600 --> 10:27.319
- Mrs. Harper...
- Mrs. Leopold.

10:27.480 --> 10:29.038
Mrs. Leopold.

10:29.200 --> 10:32.670
Did you touch your husband's body
before the police arrived?

10:32.840 --> 10:34.592
All right, yes, I pulled up his pants.

10:34.760 --> 10:37.433
- Why?
- Because it was embarrassing.

10:37.600 --> 10:40.478
There was lipstick on his hoo-hoo.

10:40.640 --> 10:42.039
- Your lipstick?
- Oh, God, no.

10:42.200 --> 10:44.270
I'd rather drink your coffee.

10:46.680 --> 10:47.999
So he was with another woman?

10:48.440 --> 10:49.953
Not necessarily.

10:50.120 --> 10:53.396
Do you have another theory
for where the lipstick came from?

10:53.920 --> 10:55.831
Have you ruled out clowns?

11:01.800 --> 11:04.837
You should check
for really big footprints.

11:08.280 --> 11:10.555
Okay, he was with another woman.

11:11.240 --> 11:14.835
- I imagine that made you pretty angry.
- I don't get angry. I get even.

11:18.080 --> 11:19.798
I mean, what are you insinuating?

11:19.960 --> 11:22.838
I'm insinuating that maybe
you caught him in the act.

11:28.360 --> 11:31.716
- Evie.
- You cheating bastard.

11:31.880 --> 11:33.472
Evie, I can explain.

11:35.680 --> 11:37.671
Evie, I can explain.

11:37.840 --> 11:39.478
I can explain.

11:48.560 --> 11:51.313
And Paris for two becomes Fiji for one.

11:52.360 --> 11:53.873
We checked your phone records.

11:54.520 --> 11:56.272
Listen, let me tell you something.

11:56.440 --> 11:58.032
I loved that man and he loved me.

11:58.200 --> 12:00.953
In fact, he loved me so much,
he didn't even ask for a prenup.

12:01.120 --> 12:03.680
And believe me, he's got money.
Big money.

12:05.240 --> 12:09.119
Well, we don't have to look very hard
to find a motive for you, do we?

12:15.520 --> 12:18.830
I'm warning you,
coffee tends to shoot through me.

12:19.160 --> 12:22.914
So if you've got a cavity search
planned, you better do it pretty quick.

12:25.320 --> 12:27.151
We don't need to do a cavity search.

12:27.320 --> 12:29.311
Can I request one?

12:32.280 --> 12:34.032
What do you know
about Teddy Leopold?

12:34.520 --> 12:36.750
I know he was hot for me.

12:37.080 --> 12:38.638
He was always flirting.

12:38.800 --> 12:41.712
Berta, this is mom's boyfriend, Teddy.
Teddy, my housekeeper Berta.

12:42.200 --> 12:45.556
- A pleasure.
- It could be if you play your cards right.

12:52.800 --> 12:54.153
You can't blame him.

12:54.320 --> 12:58.029
You gotta figure that boinking Evelyn
is like riding a bicycle over train tracks.

12:59.680 --> 13:03.719
You'll get where you're going,
but you're gonna feel every bump.

13:07.480 --> 13:10.199
- How's the hot chocolate?
- Good. I like the powdered stuff...

13:10.360 --> 13:13.875
...because there's always something
to chew on when you get to the bottom.

13:20.040 --> 13:21.393
- You got any donuts?
- Nope.

13:21.560 --> 13:22.595
- Danish?
- Nope.

13:22.760 --> 13:23.829
Pie?

13:24.800 --> 13:26.916
Look, Jake, what I wanna know is...

13:27.080 --> 13:29.310
...were you in your uncle's room
at any time today?

13:29.480 --> 13:31.630
- No, I never go in my uncle's room.
- Why not?

13:32.120 --> 13:34.680
Because all the skin mags
are in my dad's room.

13:37.080 --> 13:40.675
Okay, let me just start out by saying
I know about the illegal left-turn ticket.

13:40.840 --> 13:42.910
And I've been meaning
to take care of it...

13:43.080 --> 13:46.231
...but, you know, business has been
slow, and bills just keep coming.

13:46.400 --> 13:48.311
Of course I don't have to tell you that.

13:48.480 --> 13:50.391
Our law enforcement personnel
are underpaid.

13:50.560 --> 13:52.391
Thank you for the coffee, by the way.

13:53.640 --> 13:57.076
Cops and truck drivers, you know
your coffee. Am I going to jail?

13:59.840 --> 14:01.717
Tell me about you
and Teddy Leopold.

14:01.880 --> 14:03.950
Oh, I loved Teddy.
He was like a father to me.

14:04.120 --> 14:05.439
- Is that so?
- Yeah, yeah.

14:05.600 --> 14:08.433
He took me to Vegas,
brought me a hooker.

14:09.240 --> 14:11.151
Would any of you gentlemen
like a date?

14:11.320 --> 14:12.753
Sorry, doll, I'm taken.

14:12.920 --> 14:15.798
But I wouldn't mind
footing the bill for my two boys here.

14:16.200 --> 14:17.633
Hi, I'm Amber.

14:17.800 --> 14:18.835
I'm Tiffany.

14:21.720 --> 14:23.517
- Thanks, Daddy.
- Thanks, Daddy.

14:25.080 --> 14:26.069
A hooker?

14:26.840 --> 14:27.955
And gelato.

14:28.400 --> 14:31.358
- You got my blessing, Teddy.
- Shut up and eat your gelato.

14:32.160 --> 14:34.151
So you were happy
he married your mother?

14:34.360 --> 14:35.759
Are you kidding? I was thrilled.

14:35.920 --> 14:38.434
I planned the wedding.
And it went great.

14:38.600 --> 14:40.875
The reception not so much.

14:41.280 --> 14:43.157
Why, what happened?

14:43.840 --> 14:45.558
The groom died.

14:47.480 --> 14:49.118
Remember?

14:52.440 --> 14:54.431
Do you need to write that down?

14:55.920 --> 14:57.717
Any idea
who might have wanted him dead?

14:57.880 --> 14:59.871
No, no, everybody loved Teddy.

15:00.040 --> 15:01.473
And he was so good to my mom.

15:01.640 --> 15:03.631
It's a shame
she has to bury another husband.

15:04.200 --> 15:05.235
Another husband?

15:06.240 --> 15:09.073
Yeah, well, she's, you know,
had a bit of bad luck...

15:09.240 --> 15:11.151
...in the dead spouse department.

15:13.040 --> 15:15.918
Not that you can have good luck
in the dead spouse department.

15:16.080 --> 15:17.957
Can I have some more coffee?

15:18.920 --> 15:20.433
Who ratted me out? Was it Alan?

15:20.600 --> 15:21.589
Oh, it doesn't matter.

15:21.760 --> 15:25.230
Either one of them would throw me
under a bus for an Eskimo Pie.

15:26.160 --> 15:28.435
We'd just like to know
about your late husbands.

15:29.200 --> 15:31.794
All right. There's not much to tell.

15:31.960 --> 15:34.349
Charlie and Alan's father
died of food poisoning.

15:34.520 --> 15:35.714
Where'd he get the food?

15:36.600 --> 15:39.068
I was a young bride.
I was just learning to cook.

15:39.240 --> 15:42.710
And nobody told me
you don't keep fish in a drawer.

15:43.920 --> 15:45.876
All right, what about the others?

15:46.280 --> 15:48.396
Oh, the usual.

15:48.560 --> 15:51.950
Couple of heart attacks,
a bathtub electrocution.

15:53.960 --> 15:55.393
Why are you grilling me?

15:55.560 --> 15:58.358
I'm not the one who was
fighting with him over money.

15:58.520 --> 15:59.794
Who was?

15:59.960 --> 16:01.632
I don't understand
why you won't help.

16:01.800 --> 16:04.598
We've been through this.
I'm not gonna keep bailing you out.

16:04.760 --> 16:06.751
- But, Daddy, l...
- Don't "But Daddy" me.

16:06.920 --> 16:08.478
What am I to do?
Live on the street?

16:08.640 --> 16:10.517
You're supposed to live
within your means.

16:11.400 --> 16:13.231
I want a lawyer.

16:17.080 --> 16:18.877
Tall soy latte, no foam.

16:19.040 --> 16:21.395
Grandmommy
can't drink this cop swill anymore.

16:21.560 --> 16:24.791
- Mom, they told us to wait here.
- Well, that's why I'm sending Jake.

16:24.960 --> 16:26.996
Think of it as job training, dear.

16:27.720 --> 16:29.312
Hi, Charlie.

16:29.480 --> 16:30.674
Hey, Charlie.

16:30.840 --> 16:32.592
Hi, Charlie.

16:32.760 --> 16:34.637
Hi, Alan.

16:37.400 --> 16:39.072
I'm not the one
who's got a husband...

16:39.240 --> 16:42.038
...with someone else's lipstick
on his dipstick.

16:43.000 --> 16:44.149
Has anybody seen Courtney?

16:44.320 --> 16:45.878
She's talking to her attorney.

16:46.040 --> 16:47.359
Why does she need an attorney?

16:47.520 --> 16:51.195
GC mass spec analysis revealed
that the lipstick pigment on the body...

16:51.360 --> 16:53.669
...matches lipstick she was wearing.
- Wait.

16:53.840 --> 16:56.479
- Courtney with her own father?
- Not according to their DNA.

16:56.640 --> 16:58.392
- They're not even related.
- What?

16:58.560 --> 17:00.710
- You're kidding.
- They're con artists, grifters.

17:00.880 --> 17:02.393
Wanted in half a dozen states.

17:02.560 --> 17:06.519
His real name is Nathan Krunk
and she is Sylvia Fishman.

17:07.640 --> 17:09.198
That can't be right.

17:09.360 --> 17:10.679
I was gonna marry her.

17:10.840 --> 17:12.432
- What?
- What?

17:13.960 --> 17:17.077
We were gonna surprise you,
but I guess that ship has sailed.

17:18.120 --> 17:19.792
They've got a record of marital fraud.

17:19.960 --> 17:22.155
They pick out marks
with more money than brains...

17:22.320 --> 17:24.629
...and then take them down the aisle.

17:24.800 --> 17:26.836
You're just gonna
turn your back on me?

17:27.000 --> 17:29.434
- Don't be such a drama queen.
- You know what, forget it.

17:29.600 --> 17:31.716
- I'm out of here.
- Courtney, don't be like that.

17:32.440 --> 17:34.590
But I don't understand.

17:34.760 --> 17:37.593
Teddy didn't need money.
He was a very wealthy man.

17:37.760 --> 17:41.435
And I practically had to force Courtney
to take my $50,000.

17:49.600 --> 17:50.953
But what about his lifestyle?

17:51.120 --> 17:53.111
The private jet, the trips to Vegas?

17:53.280 --> 17:54.872
Bad checks, stolen credit cards.

17:55.040 --> 17:57.918
The reason he didn't want a prenup
is so he could get your money.

17:58.120 --> 18:01.078
But then why would Courtney
kill her own partner?

18:01.240 --> 18:02.559
She didn't.

18:02.720 --> 18:06.952
&lt;i>They were going at it hot and heavy&lt;/i>
&lt;i>and his heart gave out.&lt;/i>

18:10.840 --> 18:13.149
Yeah, I can see that happening.

18:14.520 --> 18:17.512
What threw us off at first was
the bruising on the back of his head.

18:17.680 --> 18:20.274
Then autopsy revealed
that had happened roughly 48 hours...

18:20.440 --> 18:21.839
...before time of death.

18:22.000 --> 18:24.116
Still up to get together,
so give me a call.

18:24.280 --> 18:27.113
&lt;i>I'm just sitting at home,&lt;/i>
&lt;i>reading a book.&lt;/i>

18:27.920 --> 18:29.114
That hurts.

18:29.280 --> 18:30.269
Wanna switch?

18:30.440 --> 18:33.273
Yeah, let's try banging
your head for a while.

18:35.000 --> 18:36.194
I don't believe it.

18:36.360 --> 18:39.670
She used me, she scammed me,
she took my money.

18:41.800 --> 18:43.791
- Courtney.
- What?

18:44.440 --> 18:45.873
I'll wait for you.

18:55.400 --> 18:58.198
Got a postcard from the black widow.

18:59.160 --> 19:00.434
No kidding.

19:00.600 --> 19:02.989
- How's her honeymoon going?
- Pretty good apparently.

19:03.160 --> 19:05.799
She's already met
a wealthy real-estate investor.

19:05.960 --> 19:08.554
I gotta admit, the woman's got spirit.

19:08.720 --> 19:12.679
No matter what life throws at her,
she always lands on her back.

19:16.840 --> 19:18.353
What's the matter?

19:27.960 --> 19:30.599
- Oh, Jake.
- Oh, God.

19:31.880 --> 19:34.189
That was a good one, wasn't it?

20:00.880 --> 20:02.871
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

20:03.040 --> 20:05.031
[ENGLISH]
